pkg:Evidence_v1_2_1 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.2.1 (PATCH release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PATCH: documentation-only. Adds 00-proposals/FitGap_RDODI_v1_3_0_Alignment_v1_0_0.md after rdodi-ecosystem updated to v1.98.0 / procedure v1.3.0, which adopted this package's own template-drift handover as an owner ruling: the rich sidebar/tabs/chat pattern is now RDODI's default Stage 4 deliverable, with the single flowing anchor-page and native S6 generator retained as named variations, not deprecated. The fit-gap analysis verifies, against the actual new bytes: (1) Stages 1-3 are unaffected; (2) the existing single-flowing-page Stage 4 pattern remains a legitimate, explicitly-named option; (3) a path-independent gap exists regardless of which Stage 4 approach is chosen -- the current page (built for Stage 3's prior 21-section structure) is stale against Stage 3 v1.2.0's 25 sections, and a fresh BP-D34 check (not from memory) found 2 of 25 section titles exceed the 30-char pill threshold, meaning even the existing Variation used the wrong navigation shape (flat pill-bar rather than the grouped top-bar plus sidebar the rule actually calls for at this title-length mix); (4) adopting the new Default is a substantially larger undertaking, verified against the real build instructions and schema, requiring new content (quiz, glossary) this package has never authored, not just re-templating existing prose, though proportionality against RDODI's own existing corpus instantiation confirms this package's scale is comparable and not disproportionate to attempt. Two paths are stated plainly with no default recommendation, returned to the user for a scope decision before any further Stage 4 work proceeds."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "7f2a16f0fb50c9df2c00ce92a7e1ff3e2d42f4ed4303da869d2f453419b10bd8"^^xsd:string .
